    "content": "Palm Sunday 2026, celebrated on March 29th, marks the beginning of Holy Week, commemorating Jesus Christ’s humble entry into Jerusalem on a donkey as crowds waved palm branches. It represents the start of his final journey to the crucifixion, acting as a day of joy (welcoming the King) and solemn reflection (preparing for the Passion). Key Aspects of Palm Sunday 2026 Significance: It symbolizes Jesus as the King of Peace (not war), fulfilling prophecy by riding a donkey rather than a horse. Traditions: Christians attend church services with blessed palm branches, which are often woven into crosses, used for blessings, and brought home to symbolize devotion. Synonyms/Alternate Names: Frequently called Passion Sunday in many traditions, as it initiates the Passion of Christ. Context: It marks the end of Lent (which concludes on Holy Thursday) and leads directly to Easter Sunday, which is April 5, 2026. Usage Examples & Reflections \"Hosanna!\": Songs and hymns are sung praising Jesus as the savior, reflecting the biblical welcome. Processions: Churches often hold processions where parishioners walk while waving palm branches to reenact the entrance into Jerusalem. Reflection on Humility: Religious messages focus on the contrast between the triumphant arrival and the coming suffering on the cross, emphasizing sacrifice. Palm Sunday serves as a dramatic shift in the liturgical year, moving from the reflective 40 days of Lent into the intense, final moments of Christ's life before his resurrection on Easter.",
